# User Role Permissions and Access Control

## Role Definitions

### Administrator Role
- **Full system access**: Can view and manage everything
- Can view all students, teachers, parents, and reading logs
- Can edit any reading log or user data
- Access to analytics and reporting for entire system
- Can manage all user relationships and assignments

### Teacher Role
- **Class-restricted access**: Only students in their classrooms/reading groups
- Can view and edit reading logs for their assigned students only
- Can manage parent-student relationships for their students
- Can access analytics dashboard filtered to their students
- **Cannot view**: Other teachers' students or system-wide data

### Student Role
- **Self-only access**: Can only view their own data
- Can submit new reading logs for themselves
- Can view their own reading history and progress
- **Cannot view**: Other students' data
- **Cannot edit/delete**: Submitted reading logs

### Parent Role
- **Child-restricted access**: Only their assigned children
- Can view their children's reading logs and progress
- Can submit reading logs on behalf of their children
- **Cannot view**: Other children's data
- **Cannot edit**: Existing reading logs (only submit new ones)

## Implementation Guidelines

### Database Queries and Views
- **Always filter** queries based on user relationships
- **Implement permission checks** in views before data access
- **Use Django's** `@login_required` and custom permission decorators
- **Filter querysets** by user associations (teacher-student, parent-child)

### Reading Log Management Permissions
```python
# Students: Create only, view own
if user.user_type == 'student':
    logs = ReadingLog.objects.filter(student=user)

# Teachers: CRUD for their students only
if user.user_type == 'teacher':
    student_ids = user.teacher_students.values_list('id', flat=True)
    logs = ReadingLog.objects.filter(student_id__in=student_ids)

# Parents: Create for children, view existing
if user.user_type == 'parent':
    child_ids = user.children.values_list('id', flat=True)
    logs = ReadingLog.objects.filter(student_id__in=child_ids)

# Administrators: Full access
if user.user_type == 'administrator':
    logs = ReadingLog.objects.all()
```

### Navigation and UI Rules
- **Show only relevant** menu items per user type
- **Hide admin functions** from non-admin users
- **Display contextual actions** based on user permissions
- **Use role-based** template conditionals

### Template Permission Patterns
```django
{% if user.user_type == 'teacher' %}
    <!-- Teacher-only content -->
{% elif user.user_type == 'administrator' %}
    <!-- Admin-only content -->
{% endif %}

{% if user.user_type in 'teacher,administrator' %}
    <!-- Teacher and admin content -->
{% endif %}
```

## Security Requirements

### Data Isolation
- **Never expose** data from users outside permission scope
- **Validate relationships** before allowing access
- **Use Django's** `get_object_or_404` with filtered querysets
- **Implement** proper error handling for unauthorized access

### Form and API Security
- **Validate user permissions** before processing forms
- **Filter dropdown options** based on user relationships
- **Sanitize input** and validate against user's allowed data
- **Use CSRF protection** on all forms